From 75394f4d4bf92b9261c7b29d3b1c8bbc5630edaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:26:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: IPv6 everywhere a device is named, pre-login rows
 tightened, client IPv6 for the dashboard, private /tmp

- Connections: IPv6 rows in canonical form with each LAN end named by MAC;
  Internal/External from the LAN flag; accelerator IPv6 entries skipped.
- Devices: IPv6 addresses, DHCPv6 leases bridged to their devices, DHCPv6
  reservations as host suffixes; client IP -> MAC resolves IPv6 peers too.
- get_clientlist fills a missing global IPv6 address of an online client from
  the neighbour cache (never over networkmap's value), so the dashboard and the
  stock client list show it without a reload.
- Review 2026-10-07: two pre-login rows for a removed cloud feature compiled out,
  stock proxy rows removed, archive wildcards and three retired-flow pages behind
  a login.
- Site Survey move/back files, the name map and the lock files under the /tmp
  rules of this rung; the restore's staged settings created fresh.
- basic.c removed: never compiled (the active MIME table is in web.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
